  "body": "Privately positioned at the end of a peaceful right of way in one of St Heliers' desirable coastal neighbourhoods, this beautifully presented masonry home combines contemporary style with generous family living. Enjoying all-day sun and an elevated outlook towards nearby Glover Park, this low-maintenance freehold property offers an exceptional sense of privacy, space and comfort, just moments from the coast.\r\n\r\nNorth-facing with a versatile layout, the home offers spacious living and four bedrooms, including a privately positioned upstairs master suite with ensuite. Light-filled interiors feature neutral tones, plantation shutters and generous glazing, creating a relaxed yet sophisticated atmosphere. A wide, covered balcony overlooking the leafy neighbourhood is accessed from both the open-plan family and dining area and adjoining separate lounge, providing an inviting setting for entertaining or simply unwinding. The well-appointed kitchen caters effortlessly to everyday family living and entertaining, with excellent storage and stainless steel appliances, including a gas hob.\r\n\r\nA guest powder room is located on each level, while a second bathroom downstairs services the three ground-floor bedrooms. One of these bedrooms could easily be utilised as an additional living area, with all three opening to attractive, trellis-screened patio terraces. This flexible arrangement is ideal for families of all ages, guests or those seeking additional space to work from home. Internal-access double garaging provides excellent storage and incorporates the laundry.\r\n\r\nSet on approximately 437m² of beautifully maintained freehold grounds, the property features private outdoor entertaining areas, established gardens and a fully fenced lawn with plenty of room for children and pets. A thriving vegetable garden and espaliered fruit trees add to the appeal, while a substantial covered carport provides additional parking alongside generous off-street space.\r\n\r\nZoned for Churchill Park School and Glendowie College, with St Ignatius School also nearby, this superbly located home will appeal to families, busy professionals and downsizers seeking the perfect balance of space, privacy and easy-care coastal living.\r\n\r\nSee interactive features for this property on barfoot.co.nz. Click the \"View office website\" link at the bottom of this page.",
